  "observations": [
    "At22/44px Khitan gains visible fluent pen strokes; full native stacked sample has complete bounds.",
    "Tangut and rare Han gain materially finer ink while native short strokes/counters retain their identities in these samples. Changes are deliberately smaller where dense detail constrains them.",
    "Radius smoothing, native taper caps and small injective contour flex reduce the earlier pressure clots and rigid serif contrast.",
    "31/40 sample drawings are transformed;9 source originals are explicitly retained after per-glyph or exact full-field pixel-position rejection. These are native bundled source drawings, not hidden system fallback.",
